<!-- HERO -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:812px;margin:0px auto 0;padding:88px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><h1 style="margin:0;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:60px;line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:.03em;color:#641822">GPC 2.0</h1><p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:#8B5A61">Executive reporting in Power BI</p><p style="margin:26px 0 0;max-width:520px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.5">A Power BI report that puts the key figures of ENGIE’s business units in the spotlight, and that I helped bring to life from a Figma mock-up.</p></div>
<!-- HERO IMAGE -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1100px;margin:56px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><img decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" src="images/gpc-hero.webp" alt="GPC 2.0 report displayed on a tablet." width="2138" height="736" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:4px"></div>
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1100px;margin:48px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:28px 40px;padding:28px 0;border-top:1px solid #D9D2C7;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D2C7"><div style="flex:1 1 200px;min-width:0"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:8px">Role</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.45">Product Designer, Power BI Factory: adapting the design to Power BI, keeping the report maintainable</div></div><div style="flex:1 1 200px;min-width:0"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:8px">Duration</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.45">Since October 2025, over a year</div></div><div style="flex:1 1 200px;min-width:0"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:8px">Tools</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.45">Power BI, Figma, Jira</div></div><div style="flex:1 1 200px;min-width:0"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:8px">Context</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.45">ENGIE, work-study, Power BI Factory team</div></div></div></div>
<div style="width:100%;max-width:812px;margin:88px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:12px">01 · CONTEXT</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 24px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:30px;line-height:1.25;color:#641822">A report made to expose data</h2><p style="margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6">GPC 2.0 is a report built to display data, not to modify it. It is used by the Global Business Units (GBUs), the large entities of ENGIE, mostly during their quarterly business reviews (QBR).</p><p style="margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6">The idea is to bring out the key data each GBU wants to show, and to make it easy to use in a presentation.</p></div>
<div style="width:100%;max-width:812px;margin:120px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:12px">02 · MY ROLE</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 24px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:30px;line-height:1.25;color:#641822">Making the design work in Power BI</h2><p style="margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6">When I arrived in October 2025, the mock-up had already been designed by another UX designer, and I was a beginner. My role, within the Power BI Factory team, was to find solutions to adapt the design to Power BI, and to keep the report maintainable.</p><p style="margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6">Some elements of a Figma design cannot be reproduced as they are in Power BI. For each one, I looked for a way to stay as close as possible to the mock-up, while keeping the report simple to maintain.</p></div>
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1100px;margin:56px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><a href="images/gpc-compare.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="zoom" aria-label="Open the image full size in a new tab"><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="images/gpc-compare.webp" alt="Overview page of GPC 2.0: the Figma design on the left and the Power BI report on the right, with figures blurred." width="1456" height="830" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto"></a></div><div style="width:100%;max-width:1100px;margin:14px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><p style="margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:#8B5A61">The overview page, as designed in Figma and as built in Power BI. Figures are blurred.</p></div>
<div style="width:100%;max-width:812px;margin:120px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:12px">03 · RESULT</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 24px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:30px;line-height:1.25;color:#641822">A report that stays faithful to the mock-up</h2><p style="margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6">Today the report is very close to the Figma design, which I consider a real success, and the feedback has been very positive.</p></div>
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1100px;margin:120px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><h2 style="margin:0 0 28px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:28px;color:#641822">What I take away</h2><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px"><div style="flex:1 1 280px;min-width:0;border-top:2px solid #641822;padding-top:18px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:500">Adapting a design to a tool starts with knowing the tool’s limits.</p></div><div style="flex:1 1 280px;min-width:0;border-top:2px solid #641822;padding-top:18px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:500">A good compromise keeps the purpose of a component, even when its shape changes.</p></div><div style="flex:1 1 280px;min-width:0;border-top:2px solid #641822;padding-top:18px"><p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:500">A report that stays close to its mock-up is easier to maintain and to explain.</p></div></div></div>
<div style="width:100%;max-width:812px;margin:56px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><p style="margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:#8B5A61;border-left:2px solid #D9D2C7;padding-left:16px">Figures are blurred and some details are left out, because the report is internal to ENGIE.</p></div>
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1100px;margin:96px auto 0;padding:0px 24px 0;box-sizing:border-box"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:14px">Next project</div><a href="/rse" style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;border-top:1px solid #D9D2C7;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D2C7;padding:28px 0;text-decoration:none;color:#641822"><div style="flex:1 1 360px;min-width:0"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:26px;margin-bottom:8px">RSE Environnement</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;max-width:520px">Two redesigns of ENGIE’s climate and environmental risk reports in Power BI.</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-weight:600;font-size:15px">View case study<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="#641822" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8h12M9 3l5 5-5 5"></path></svg></span></a></div>
</main>
